writingTasks.instructions:
You cannot attend the team briefing that is scheduled for tomorrow morning at 09:00. Leave a note for your colleague Alex in which you:
• explain why you cannot be there;
• ask Alex to take notes on your behalf;
• suggest a specific time to meet so Alex can brief you afterwards.

Write your note in 50–100 words.

You are a staff officer. Your unit has just been assigned an unexpected operational task running from 3 to 14 November, which directly conflicts with a professional development course you were scheduled to attend from 7 to 11 November.

Write a formal email to the course coordinator, Lieutenant Colonel Martinez, in which you:
• state the reason for your request and the dates affected;
• formally request a deferral to the next available course date;
• express your continued commitment to completing the requirement;
• offer to provide any documentation needed.

Write 150–250 words. Use appropriate email conventions (subject line, salutation, sign-off).

Choose ONE of the following three questions and write an analytical essay in response. Your essay must:
• state a clear thesis in the introduction;
• develop your argument across at least two body paragraphs, using evidence and reasoning;
• include at least one substantive concession to a counter-argument;
• end with a conclusion that answers the question directly.
